{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe","id":1102336,"title":"Are the Hsien still part of (but not really) the Changeling universe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-10T12:57:37-07:00","id":1102336,"title":"Are the Hsien still part of (but not really) the Changeling universe?","content":"Are the Hsien still a thing in Changeling 20? I never really understood them and am not sure why the exist or what eastern Fae are like. Did no Chimera in The East ever get a promotion from the Dreaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T13:22:14-07:00","id":1102343,"title":"","content":"Yes, they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T13:24:09-07:00","id":1102344,"title":"","content":"They are in fact substantially more playable now than they were previously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:17:04-07:00","id":1102354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102344#post1102344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are in fact substantially more playable now than they were previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Can you give me details about them and the Eastern Dreaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:17:21-07:00","id":1102377,"title":"","content":"They still have nothing to do with the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:19:31-07:00","id":1102378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102377#post1102377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They still have nothing to do with the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they even have Fae/Chimera/The Dreaming in the East?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:24:48-07:00","id":1102380,"title":"","content":"They say nothing about them. My thought is they even have their own Changelings, just nothing is mentioned in canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:28:35-07:00","id":1102382,"title":"","content":"Don't Hsien still need to be enchanted to see the changeling Miens and chimera? I see them as spin offs of Dark Age Fae like changeling, but not tied to dreams.<br /> <br /> In fact maybe Heaven is in the Dreaming, that is were all the other God Heavens of the Fae seem to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T16:34:16-07:00","id":1102392,"title":"","content":"I think Heaven is supposed to be the High Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T20:26:19-07:00","id":1102421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102392#post1102392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Heaven is supposed to be the High Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well its accessable via umbral powers so presumably its up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T02:35:24-07:00","id":1102471,"title":"","content":"Deep Umbra and Deep Dreaming are very similar places, and I reckon are the same realm just different sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T03:42:47-07:00","id":1102477,"title":"","content":"I treat eastern supernaturals as their own setting, anyone is free to use or ignore as they see fit.<br /> <br /> Kindred to Kindred of the East for me like Lupines to Kindred, etc. In the same vein I ignore the existence of Fera when I read about Garou.<br /> <br /> You are free to crossover, but there is no (nor cannot be) a right way to crossover. All inconsistencies are for you to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-11-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T12:37:15-07:00","id":1102580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102477#post1102477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I treat eastern supernaturals as their own setting, anyone is free to use or ignore as they see fit.<br /> <br /> Kindred to Kindred of the East for me like Lupines to Kindred, etc. In the same vein I ignore the existence of Fera when I read about Garou.<br /> <br /> You are free to crossover, but there is nor cannot be right way to crossover. All inconsistencies are for you to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You live in an inconsistant universe where people believe radically different things about how it functions. And yet you putter on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:13:08-07:00","id":1102593,"title":"","content":"What's surely inconsistent that's our knowledge of the universe, if you'd allow me to be pedantic. As for the universe itself, to say it's inconsistent is a very bold claim.<br /> <br /> I have nothing more to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T07:29:48-07:00","id":1103126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously? The Dreaming must exist globally, it's the realm of dreams. Why even mention them in <i>Changeling: The Dreaming</i> if they're not Dreaming-related?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T07:46:04-07:00","id":1103135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102477#post1102477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I treat eastern supernaturals as their own setting, anyone is free to use or ignore as they see fit.<br /> <br /> Kindred to Kindred of the East for me like Lupines to Kindred, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>...huh?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the same vein I ignore the existence of Fera when I read about Garou. </div> </div> </div>That would be a bit of an error, since their existence and sorry state is one of the reasons why the Garou are in a gigantic clusterfuck, to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are free to crossover, but there is no (nor cannot be) a right way to crossover. All inconsistencies are for you to deal with. </div> </div> </div>I think that there could be right and wrong ways to interpret stats from other games. The way Vampire interprets Rank and Pure Breed from Werewolf, for example, is as wrong as wrong can be, and should really be changed in this world that exists over twenty years after The Chaos Factor..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:08:21-07:00","id":1103184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1103135#post1103135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actively ignore VtM lore, when running a KotE chronicle. Western vampires, that deal with kuei-jin are mysterious and undefined.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would be a bit of an error, since their existence and sorry state is one of the reasons why the Garou are in a gigantic clusterfuck, to say the least. </div> </div> </div>So, what you're saying is that I play Roleplaying Game wrong? But why should I care? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that there could be right and wrong ways to interpret stats from other games. The way Vampire interprets Rank and Pure Breed from Werewolf, for example, is as wrong as wrong can be, and should really be changed in this world that exists over twenty years after The Chaos Factor.. </div> </div> </div>But why should it be important, if all I want to have fun with my friends? Or any Storyteller, for that matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:10:03-07:00","id":1103186,"title":"","content":"Though I do like the Hsien, I dont find them a good fit for mixed chronicles. The inability to leave the Autumn world is particularly frustrating story wise, as travel into the Dreaming is always a possibility in my games.<br /> <br /> And what of the kithain, gallain or even thallain born into Asian families? Also, Japanese Yokai stories are more in tune with the Dreaming, with some aspects leaning towards Menehune, and Nunehi mechanics more than Hsien and Wu Tan Alchemy. So I think a special focus on Yokai is in order.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-13-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:55:32-07:00","id":1103209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1103184#post1103184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actively ignore VtM lore, when running a KotE chronicle. Western vampires, that deal with kuei-jin are mysterious and undefined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what you're saying is that I play Roleplaying Game wrong? But why should I care? </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that Fera are much more tightly integrated with the main body of Werewolf than Gui Ren and Hsien are with their respective games, both on the story front and the mechanical presentation. They have mostly the same concerns and they learn Gifts and rites in about the same way, making them closer to the &quot;main play experience&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But why should it be important, if all I want to have fun with my friends? Or any Storyteller, for that matter? </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about official rules, here. What we have now in the way of guidelines on the books are extremely bizarre choices for crossover that don't make any sense at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T12:45:17-07:00","id":1103236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1103209#post1103209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that Fera are much more tightly integrated with the main body of Werewolf than Gui Ren and Hsien are with their respective games, both on the story front and the mechanical presentation. They have mostly the same concerns and they learn Gifts and rites in about the same way, making them closer to the &quot;main play experience&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my bad - I should've clarified - in this case, I don't say, that Fera are badly integrated. It's just that I like my Werewolf experience without cree- wererats and werespiders, or whatever. Wolves and their core mythos are good enough for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm talking about official rules, here. What we have now in the way of guidelines on the books are extremely bizarre choices for a crossover that don't make any sense at all. </div> </div> </div>Well, I abandoned all my hopes for official rules to be sufficient to run a WoD game years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-13-2017, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T14:20:00-07:00","id":1103273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? After so many people hated that about them in the original edition? I thought the fact they were being included meant they were going to be re-done right. Onyx Path has made other significant changes where appropriate between editions of games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think I either plan to run LoEMD as it's own separate thing or just ignore it and pretend, there are usual Dreaming stuff with gallain, kiths and chimerae. Only borrowing and changing stuff here and there for my needs if necessary. It certainly won't be a masterpiece game setting, but who cares? As long as players and me have fun.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this isn't a solution for everybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T00:47:43-07:00","id":1103410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102593#post1102593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's surely inconsistent that's our knowledge of the universe, if you'd allow me to be pedantic. As for the universe itself, to say it's inconsistent is a very bold claim.<br /> <br /> I have nothing more to add.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll accept the Pedantic. We are constantly revising our understanding of the universe. And people have for all of history functioned with incomplete and misunderstood views of the world. A consistant setting in my mind would be HIGHLY unrealistic, it shows its obvious creation as a fictional setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:54:39-07:00","id":1104026,"title":"","content":"The C20 Hsien are more playable than before, but still vague in some surprisingly key places. If you squint, it can all be interpreted in a pro-integration light.<br /> <br /> For example: The text says that the Hsien are unrelated to dreams or the Dreaming, but it's clear that they rely so heavily on human hopes and fears -- which they call prayers-- that to an outside observer, Yugen (which is described as &quot;ineffable and brilliant&quot;) is basically Glamour in all but name.<br /> <br /> The text also says nothing about chimerical reality-- doesn't say Hsien don't see it, or don't believe in it, nothing. I don't think the author even uses the word &quot;chimerical&quot; once. For word count reasons or otherwise, they simply don't describe how the Hsien see the world.<br /> <br /> There's ALSO no information given on how the Wani forms of the Hsien actually work: how they are activated or deactivated, what happens when a mortal sees the Wani form, and so on. It's a big blank.<br /> <br /> So, given all that information, the Hsien could be interpreted as fae just like the Kithain, just under a *vastly* different Changeling Way. Their version transfers fae souls to stillborn and dying humans, and their mien is either Wyrd-active or completely hidden; there's no passive form. The Hsien, by canon, are completely barred from any spirit world (including the Dreaming), but they could arguably see the Autumn World in its chimerical glory just fine-- They just don't connect it to &quot;dreams,&quot; and why would they? They're starting from the assumption that everything is powered by &quot;prayers.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only outright reinterpretation necessary would be the Hsiens' relationship to Banality. Personally, just like the Wani form, I would say that Hsien suffer from an &quot;all-or-nothing&quot; form of Banality. Rather than tracking Banality points and dealing with concepts like Undoing, the Hsien simply die quickly. Their mortal lives are brilliant and, with few exceptions, tragically brief.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that the revised Hsien are all gravy. I think their powers and kiths are too limited in scope, so I would personally make sweeping changes there. If anyone's interested, I can go into more detail on that... But as far as running on just the text alone, I don't think it's hard at all to have Kithain and Hsien together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:17:15-07:00","id":1104381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1102471#post1102471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deep Umbra and Deep Dreaming are very similar places, and I reckon are the same realm just different sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Both the Dreaming and the Umbra connect to the same Realms like the Abyss, Hollow Earth, Arcadia Gateway etc. Its just each group has a different way of perceiving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T19:50:05-07:00","id":1104588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1104381#post1104381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Both the Dreaming and the Umbra connect to the same Realms like the Abyss, Hollow Earth, Arcadia Gateway etc. Its just each group has a different way of perceiving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah the Hollow Earth is serious business. That's why being a Etherite is apparently so Banal you can't buy any Fae related merits(Stupid book of secrets)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T03:54:37-07:00","id":1104676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1104588#post1104588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah the Hollow Earth is serious business. That's why being a Etherite is apparently so Banal you can't buy any Fae related merits(Stupid book of secrets)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nocker Kithbook mentions the Hollow Earth as a Realm they visit. And they are big fans of the Sons of Ether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T10:43:41-07:00","id":1104781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inconsistency as to whether science/scifi is good or bad, glamorous or banal strikes again.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're presented as being potential sources of Glamour in C20, but if someone is just going through the motions or attempting to crush possibilities, it's not going to be very glamorous. And Etherites are former technocrats with many of the trappings of the seedy underbelly of academia, so if they get embroiled in competition like, say, the one you saw with Cope vs. Marsh, things can get rather Banal quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:45:01-07:00","id":1104803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inconsistency as to whether science/scifi is good or bad, glamorous or banal strikes again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always take it that administration is the banal part. Especially when its lesser minds with pet theories in charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T03:49:05-07:00","id":1105023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1104026#post1104026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The C20 Hsien are more playable than before, but still vague in some surprisingly key places. If you squint, it can all be interpreted in a pro-integration light.<br /> <br /> For example: The text says that the Hsien are unrelated to dreams or the Dreaming, but it's clear that they rely so heavily on human hopes and fears -- which they call prayers-- that to an outside observer, Yugen (which is described as &amp;quot;ineffable and brilliant&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> is basically Glamour in all but name.<br /> <br /> The text also says nothing about chimerical reality-- doesn't say Hsien don't see it, or don't believe in it, nothing. I don't think the author even uses the word &amp;quot;chimerical&amp;quot; once. For word count reasons or otherwise, they simply don't describe how the Hsien see the world.<br /> <br /> There's ALSO no information given on how the Wani forms of the Hsien actually work: how they are activated or deactivated, what happens when a mortal sees the Wani form, and so on. It's a big blank.<br /> <br /> So, given all that information, the Hsien could be interpreted as fae just like the Kithain, just under a *vastly* different Changeling Way. Their version transfers fae souls to stillborn and dying humans, and their mien is either Wyrd-active or completely hidden; there's no passive form. The Hsien, by canon, are completely barred from any spirit world (including the Dreaming), but they could arguably see the Autumn World in its chimerical glory just fine-- They just don't connect it to &amp;quot;dreams,&amp;quot; and why would they? They're starting from the assumption that everything is powered by &amp;quot;prayers.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The only outright reinterpretation necessary would be the Hsiens' relationship to Banality. Personally, just like the Wani form, I would say that Hsien suffer from an &amp;quot;all-or-nothing&amp;quot; form of Banality. Rather than tracking Banality points and dealing with concepts like Undoing, the Hsien simply die quickly. Their mortal lives are brilliant and, with few exceptions, tragically brief.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that the revised Hsien are all gravy. I think their powers and kiths are too limited in scope, so I would personally make sweeping changes there. If anyone's interested, I can go into more detail on that... But as far as running on just the text alone, I don't think it's hard at all to have Kithain and Hsien together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, please do go into more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T09:09:32-07:00","id":1105092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105023#post1105023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, please do go into more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure thing. Just like everything I mentioned in my last post, I'd aim for simplicity and compatibility first.<br /> <br /> The current powers of the Hsien present themselves as flexible and potent, but in practice, the system does a poor job of executing effects that starting players might actually want. What elemental alchemy does a Tanuki use to disguise themselves as a local politician, or to shapechange into a young man's pillow for dubious overnight purposes? What does a Sui-jen noble use to convince a nightclub bouncer to tell her the truth about a mysterious event? I know it can all eventually be figured out using the Wu Tan, but not efficiently or all that well.<br /> <br /> It turns out that, for the right mix of potency, flexibility <i>and</i> concrete effects that players can hold onto, the best system is actually C20's redesigned Arts and Realms. Thus, I would have the Hsien use basically the same system as the Kithain.<br /> <br /> That said, the Arts have some pesky western biases. Some powers of the Art of Autumn, especially the ones that involve fear and ghosts, would make more sense in Japan as part of the &quot;Art of Summer.&quot; In places like Korea and China that still honor harvest festivals, the &quot;Art of Autumn&quot; would actually have some effects associated with the western Art of Spring. The Art of Metamorphosis is mostly fine, but the ability to transform into inanimate objects is arguably just as important in East Asian mythology-- And those are just a few examples.<br /> <br /> To solve this, I would suggest that the Hsien have access to alternative cantrip levels. Of course, to them they aren't &quot;alternate&quot;-- To the Hsien, the Kithain are strange cousins who can shapeshift just fine, but somehow or other they're not able to turn into umbrellas or cabinets, which everyone should be able to do. A Hsien will use Wayfare to walk on water and up walls like a wushu movie, and when their Kithain friends need to Unleash to do the same, they'll just shrug and chalk it up to the way they were taught.<br /> <br /> As for the kiths (no idea why they're called kwannon-jin-- a reference to the Bodhisattva of Mercy? Maybe kannon-jin would be better then):<br /> <br /> I find the fundamental split between elements and animals to be interesting and evocative, and it should be kept. To encompass the possibilities of myth and legend, though, they just need to be opened up a <i>lot</i> more instead of hewing to an artificial five-element scheme. Players complain that they can't be tengu or kappa or oni, and this would solve the issue nicely: Perhaps the kappa is a unique form of water noble, or a misunderstood form of commoner based on river turtles. Perhaps an oni is an elemental noble of fire and earth-- or it could just as easily be a strange mixture of tiger and bear and wolf, a type of commoner that embodies the wild woods.<br /> <br /> Basically, just as no human myth fully embodies the Houses of the Sidhe, or the way Sluagh or Nockers work, human myths should also be a slightly warped take on the elemental nobles and animal commoners, who are as varied as all the things on earth. That's how I would run the Hsien to my satisfaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T12:53:08-07:00","id":1105147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105092#post1105092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Art of Metamorphosis is mostly fine, but the ability to transform into inanimate objects is arguably just as important in East Asian mythology</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you share an example? Specifically a transformation, not un umbrella gaining a spirit over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105092#post1105092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find the fundamental split between elements and animals to be interesting and evocative, and it should be kept.</div> </div> </div> </div> What would you think about a split between kami and y\u014dkai, instead? Although a lot of kami <i>are </i>related to elements and nature, sometimes more broadly and sometimes more narrowly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-18-2017, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T12:56:37-07:00","id":1105150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105147#post1105147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you share an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Wukung learned multiple transformation alchemies from a sage. And yokai like tanuki, tengu, and kitsune have both illusions and transformations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T13:18:20-07:00","id":1105162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105150#post1105150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yokai like tanuki, tengu, and kitsune have both illusions and transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transformations into inanimate things, you mean?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T13:36:26-07:00","id":1105166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105162#post1105162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Transformations into inanimate things, you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you remember Super MARIO 3 or Pompoko?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T13:45:12-07:00","id":1105167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105147#post1105147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you share an example? Specifically a transformation, not un umbrella gaining a spirit over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to point you to some Korean stories (specifically thinking of something turning into a river), but now that I'm looking for them I can't find anything... Sorry for the weak example, but hopefully the overall idea still stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105147#post1105147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What would you think about a split between kami and y\u014dkai, instead? Although a lot of kami <i>are </i>related to elements and nature, sometimes more broadly and sometimes more narrowly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kami being the nobles and yokai being the commoners? That's a good idea for Japan, I'd say. I think the current name for nobles, &quot;Kamuii,&quot; is from Hokkaido, so it's not even too much of a stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T14:08:56-07:00","id":1105173,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't remove the Wu Tan; but I could see them operating alongside existing Arts. In addition to retaining a flavorful alchemy system, that would be one less thing about their Kiths that wouldn't need to be replaced \u2014 though you'd still have to go through and select which Realm each has an Affinity with (when using the standard Arts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T14:29:13-07:00","id":1105178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105166#post1105166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you remember Super MARIO 3 or Pompoko?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have a hard time remembering something, I've never interacted before, just like anyone else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though, I see the appeal of equating modern works of Japanese media and historic folklore. I have thought about parallels between urban legends originated from Japan and stories about vengeful or malicious y\u014dkai, so while definitely a stretch it's still a curious direction.<br /> <br /> That aside, do you have more historical accounts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-18-2017, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T14:35:21-07:00","id":1105180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105167#post1105167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to point you to some Korean stories (specifically thinking of something turning into a river), but now that I'm looking for them I can't find anything... Sorry for the weak example, but hopefully the overall idea still stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Sun Wukong example was good. He had been taught 72 woundrous transformations, and while I recall most if not all transformations all of the characters do throughout the Journey to the West, I find it feasible, that they could transform into inanimate objects, just as easily, even if I can't remember if there was a case.<br /> <br /> What I am curious, if there was a case in Japan or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-18-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T21:38:10-07:00","id":1105280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105180#post1105180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I am curious, if there was a case in Japan or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>That, I definitely couldn't tell you for sure. I suspect Japan's myths are mostly the other way around-- Though of course, who's to say that legends of tsukumogami aren't just a human distortion of what the Hsien actually do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105173#post1105173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't remove the Wu Tan; but I could see them operating alongside existing Arts. In addition to retaining a flavorful alchemy system, that would be one less thing about their Kiths that wouldn't need to be replaced \u2014 though you'd still have to go through and select which Realm each has an Affinity with (when using the standard Arts).</div> </div> </div> </div>An alternate idea I had was to convert Elemental Alchemy into five Arts, with Internal Alchemy also divided into five Arts, like so:<br /> <br /> Way of the Warrior - Dragon's Ire<br /> Way of the Entertainer - Chicanery<br /> Way of the Merchant - Contracts<br /> Way of the Prince - Sovereign<br /> Way of the Farmer - unsure on this one<br /> <br /> The reason being that if Internal Alchemy is a pathway back to heaven's grace, and the Hsien originally lost the favor of heaven by burying their heads in the sand and ignoring the world, then perhaps they need to understand different ways of being human. But as you can imagine, I saw the work ahead to make this happen and decided it wasn't a very elegant solution.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Wu Tan and Nei Tan could be folded together into a unique ritual subsystem for Hsien. It's no more strange than the unique subsystems of the Dark-Kin or Inanimae. I'll have to mull it over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T00:08:41-07:00","id":1105300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105280#post1105280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That, I definitely couldn't tell you for sure. I suspect Japan's myths are mostly the other way around-- Though of course, who's to say that legends of tsukumogami aren't just a human distortion of what the Hsien actually do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I contemplated that kind of justification, but it doesn't sit well with me.<br /> <br /> Look.<br /> <br /> Old things, that grow and mature into sentience with time and service? Each crack and imperfection - embraced - to become part of the thing's unique personality? Robot dogs, popular in the 00s - given proper burial rituals in Shinto temples on request of their owners, to join the host of local kami? Things, abandonded and left without proper and deserved care might come for you to teach you a lesson/terrify you to death?<br /> <br /> If this's not a conscious effort to help Chimerae born - on a cultural level - I don't know what is. =)<br /> <br /> I'm not against transformation into inanimate objects, per se. But not at the cost of actually cool things about this folklore, that do fit nicely into Changeling setting (while some others - don't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-19-2017, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T01:14:35-07:00","id":1105310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105178#post1105178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have a hard time remembering something, I've never interacted before, just like anyone else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though, I see the appeal of equating modern works of Japanese media and historic folklore. I have thought about parallels between urban legends originated from Japan and stories about vengeful or malicious y\u014dkai, so while definitely a stretch it's still a curious direction.<br /> <br /> That aside, do you have more historical accounts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Literally look up any story of tanuki, they are specifically shapeshifters with magical scrotums for tells. All there stories are about them shapeshifting into both people and objects, from statues to household items. Here is one random mention of it in a scholarly source.<a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1890/154-9295-10.4.224/full\" target=\"_blank\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/1...-10.4.224/full</a><br /> <br /> Kitsune are also able to transform as are a few other spirits and such. I don't know what to tell you though you want me to list off books, often in a language I don't really speak? <br /> <a href=\"http://Hino, Iwao (2006). D\u014dbutsu y\u014dkaitan (\u52d5\u7269\u5996\u602a\u8b5a?). 2. Ch\u016b\u014d K\u014dron Shinsha. ISBN 978-4-12-204792-1\" target=\"_blank\">http://Hino, Iwao (2006). D\u014dbutsu y\u014d...-4-12-204792-1</a><br /> <br /> I mean these are folktales look up any of these creatures and you may find stories where they use different powers. I mean most changeling kiths don't have stories where they turn into rocks, and logs, many do but I wouldn't say most. The Arts are powers displayed by various things rather then specifically one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T03:01:08-07:00","id":1105326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105310#post1105310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Literally look up any story of tanuki, they are specifically shapeshifters with magical scrotums for tells. All there stories are about them shapeshifting into both people and objects, from statues to household items. Here is one random mention of it in a scholarly source.<a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1890/154-9295-10.4.224/full\" target=\"_blank\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/1...-10.4.224/full</a><br /> <br /> Kitsune are also able to transform as are a few other spirits and such. I don't know what to tell you though you want me to list off books, often in a language I don't really speak? <br /> <a href=\"http://Hino, Iwao (2006). D\u014dbutsu y\u014dkaitan (\u52d5\u7269\u5996\u602a\u8b5a?). 2. Ch\u016b\u014d K\u014dron Shinsha. ISBN 978-4-12-204792-1\" target=\"_blank\">http://Hino, Iwao (2006). D\u014dbutsu y\u014d...-4-12-204792-1</a><br /> <br /> I mean these are folktales look up any of these creatures and you may find stories where they use different powers. I mean most changeling kiths don't have stories where they turn into rocks, and logs, many do but I wouldn't say most. The Arts are powers displayed by various things rather then specifically one thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may have a point here. I'll consider.<br /> <br /> Thanks for links.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-19-2017, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:38:51-07:00","id":1105365,"title":"","content":"More Asian inspired Denizens are in order I think. The mechanics for such would better suit than the present Hsien in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:17:46-07:00","id":1105464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105365#post1105365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More Asian inspired Denizens are in order I think. The mechanics for such would better suit than the present Hsien in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. I personally don't care much for the Dark-kin's three aria system, as well as their lack of a default physical body.<br /> <br /> I think if one were to convert the Hsien entirely to existing templates, it would be interesting and fun to have Inanimae as the &quot;nobles&quot;/kamuii of East Asia, while &quot;commoners&quot;/hirayanu are human-born Changelings. You would make them exactly the same as standard Inanimae and Kithain, with access to the same power sets and template abilities, just under different societal forces. Combined with the make-your-own-kith system in C20, it's about as easy and elegant as it gets.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what template you use, it's surprisingly simple to keep the fundamental Hsien concepts (Yugen, heavenly mandate, the tense relations with eastern vampires, etc) largely as-is. Banality is the new element, but it would take on connotations of spiritual void and disconnection with the divine, which is arguably even clearer than what Banality means in the West.<br /> <br /> I like the Hsien template in a lot of ways, but tinkering like this is fun too. I see the merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:33:42-07:00","id":1105468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105464#post1105464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting idea. I personally don't care much for the Dark-kin's three aria system, as well as their lack of a default physical body.<br /> <br /> I think if one were to convert the Hsien entirely to existing templates, it would be interesting and fun to have Inanimae as the &quot;nobles&quot;/kamuii of East Asia, while &quot;commoners&quot;/hirayanu are human-born Changelings. You would make them exactly the same as standard Inanimae and Kithain, with access to the same power sets and template abilities, just under different societal forces. Combined with the make-your-own-kith system in C20, it's about as easy and elegant as it gets.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what template you use, it's surprisingly simple to keep the fundamental Hsien concepts (Yugen, heavenly mandate, the tense relations with eastern vampires, etc) largely as-is. Banality is the new element, but it would take on connotations of spiritual void and disconnection with the divine, which is arguably even clearer than what Banality means in the West.<br /> <br /> I like the Hsien template in a lot of ways, but tinkering like this is fun too. I see the merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Inanimae are favorites of mine, and I am pleased by their treatment in C20. So I am all for their expansion, especially in an Asion mode. Strikes me that they would have remained active during the Interregnum, growing strong indeed. This could be a cool kickoff towards conflict with House Varick, as they would resent being controlled by these Russian Sidhe. <br /> <br /> On a similar note, many of the Asian fae seem like they could be Fairy Animals rather than human born. Badgers, Cats, Frogs, etc. And more than a few Krofted Inanimae can be found in the form of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukumogami\" target=\"_blank\">Tsukumogami </a>creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T08:52:50-07:00","id":1105713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105468#post1105468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a similar note, many of the Asian fae seem like they could be Fairy Animals rather than human born. Badgers, Cats, Frogs, etc. And more than a few Krofted Inanimae can be found in the form of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukumogami\" target=\"_blank\">Tsukumogami </a>creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if East Asia had virtually no human-born fae at all-- Just Inanimae and creatures similar to the Inanimae who anchor themselves to animals. That would go a long way toward explaining why they don't quite &quot;get&quot; their western cousins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:29:07-07:00","id":1105729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105713#post1105713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine if East Asia had virtually no human-born fae at all-- Just Inanimae and creatures similar to the Inanimae who anchor themselves to animals. That would go a long way toward explaining why they don't quite &quot;get&quot; their western cousins.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are quite a few y\u014dkai, that are humanoid in nature...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:57:12-07:00","id":1105743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105729#post1105729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are quite a few y\u014dkai, that are humanoid in nature...</div> </div> </div> </div>True, which is what husks might be for. It's just an idea-- I'm much more in favor of an Inanimae-noble/Changeling-commoner split, if one has to imagine something other than the existing Hsien. I prefer simple solutions that maintain the text as-is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:47:01-07:00","id":1105762,"title":"","content":"Likewise. What I've liked about Hsienfan's suggestions, starting with his(?) first post here, is that they've brought the Hsien into the fold instead of replacing them with something else; and If much rather she(?) continue that premise rather than scrapping the Hsien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:30:32-07:00","id":1106167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1105762#post1105762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise. What I've liked about Hsienfan's suggestions, starting with his(?) first post here, is that they've brought the Hsien into the fold instead of replacing them with something else; and If much rather she(?) continue that premise rather than scrapping the Hsien.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let's go back to that. I think if the world of Changeling: the Dreaming has room for Inanimae, Dark-kin, &quot;tribal&quot; fae and Thallain, it surely has room for the Hsien.<br /> <br /> Now that I've had a few posts to think, I'm in favor of bringing the Hsien fundamentally in line with the other templates, while keeping their uniqueness as unchanged as possible. To me, this means the following additions to the Hsien template:<ul><li>A Permanent and Temporary Yugen track, which is the same as Glamour.</li> <li>A Permanent and Temporary Banality track (which, if we got to rename, I'd vote for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kegare\" target=\"_blank\">Kegare</a>).</li> <li>The ability to learn Arts and Realms, even if it isn't their default power set.</li> <li>The explicit ability to see and interact with chimerical reality.</li> </ul>The Hsien template's unique elements, lifted from the C20 text, would be:<ul><li>The kun shou, which requires that they incarnate in the bodies of the dying rather than in unborn children.</li> <li>The hotei and wani forms, which Hsien can apparently switch between at no cost, reflexively. The wani form triggers the Mists, and they get no chimerical seeming.</li> <li>Wu Tan, their default powers. Just as with Arts and Realms, any human-born fae (or Mannikin) should theoretically be able to learn Hsien alchemy, if they got the right teacher.</li> <li>Yin and Yang, which technically everyone has, but non-Hsien must be taught to awaken. A prerequisite for learning Wu Tan. (In systems terms, non-Hsien should only be able to buy chi values with freebies or experience.)</li> <li>The inability to go into any spirit world, unless the Hsien gets assistance or achieves enlightenment.</li> </ul>After all that's done, the only thing remaining on my wish list would be a &quot;How Do You DO That?&quot; style manual for alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:55:10-07:00","id":1106211,"title":"","content":"How important is it that the hotei and want forms be one-at-a-time? That is, what would break if they worked exactly like a Kithain's two forms with the hotei form being the one that mortals normally see while the wani form is the one seen by those who can see Chimerical Reality? (My thoughts on why Lo8MD did it the way they did later; I've been summoned by work, and must go for now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:37:47-07:00","id":1106234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106211#post1106211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How important is it that the hotei and want forms be one-at-a-time? That is, what would break if they worked exactly like a Kithain's two forms with the hotei form being the one that mortals normally see while the wani form is the one seen by those who can see Chimerical Reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything would break. From what I can tell, the one-at-a-time forms are part of the Hsien's in-setting need to hide from their enemies, but not a mechanical necessity. It might even be ideal for mixed chronicles just to say they work like the Kithain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:48:20-07:00","id":1106237,"title":"","content":"Who are the enemies that they're hiding from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T14:08:26-07:00","id":1106249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106237#post1106237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the enemies that they're hiding from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly I think of the eastern vampires/Wan Kuei, who find Yugen delicious and addicting. The C20 text isn't specific, but it alludes to other beings who would consume the Hsien given half a chance.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could argue that if the Hsien have chimerical aspects just like other fae, then that's all the camouflage they need. It would make integrating the Hsien even easier, which I'm not opposed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T13:08:05-07:00","id":1106706,"title":"","content":"Can they enter the Dreaming without a Jade key? Or has that flaw been removed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T14:29:42-07:00","id":1106736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106706#post1106706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they enter the Dreaming without a Jade key? Or has that flaw been removed?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the C20 writeup, they still need the Jade Key to go into a spirit realm... But there are also references elsewhere to Hsien just hanging around markets in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Near Dreaming is an exception, and at the gateway to trods going deeper/elsewhere, the Hsien get waylaid by heavenly punishment. Or perhaps enlightenment is relatively easy for the Hsien to obtain-- either that, or the enlightened really get around and get noticed by foreign gallain.<br /> <br /> It's a mystery, sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T14:52:29-07:00","id":1106744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106736#post1106736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the C20 writeup, they still need the Jade Key to go into a spirit realm... But there are also references elsewhere to Hsien just hanging around markets in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Near Dreaming is an exception, and at the gateway to trods going deeper/elsewhere, the Hsien get waylaid by heavenly punishment. Or perhaps enlightenment is relatively easy for the Hsien to obtain-- either that, or the enlightened really get around and get noticed by foreign gallain.<br /> <br /> It's a mystery, sadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a house rule, I would say that the Near Dreaming and maybe the Yomi worlds would be allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T15:09:30-07:00","id":1106750,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: the Dreaming is not the Umbra. Not sure how relevant that is; but there you go. <br /> <br /> (The closest we get to a connection between the Dreaming and the Umbra is that the various books on the Umbra speak of a Zone called the Maya, which many identify with the Dreaming. But bear in mind that the Digital Web is also described as a Zone; and as Mage fans know, the Digital Web is definitely not in the Umbra. \u201cZones\u201d are best thought of as places that aren't spirit worlds, but which have connections to the Spirit Worlds \u2014 much like the material world isn't a Spirit world, but has connections to the Spirit Worlds.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:33:23-07:00","id":1106770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106750#post1106750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: the Dreaming is not the Umbra. Not sure how relevant that is; but there you go. <br /> <br /> (The closest we get to a connection between the Dreaming and the Umbra is that the various books on the Umbra speak of a Zone called the Maya, which many identify with the Dreaming. But bear in mind that the Digital Web is also described as a Zone; and as Mage fans know, the Digital Web is definitely not in the Umbra. \u201cZones\u201d are best thought of as places that aren't spirit worlds, but which have connections to the Spirit Worlds \u2014 much like the material world isn't a Spirit world, but has connections to the Spirit Worlds.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know this-- That bit of information is a game-changer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T17:05:02-07:00","id":1106788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106770#post1106770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not know this-- That bit of information is a game-changer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its all vague and contradictory. Appropriate for something related to dreams. The Maya are said to be pocket universes, ruled by powerful Umbrood called the Oneiroi. House Scathach had access to these worlds during the Interregnum.<br /> <br /> There is also other places mentioned that sound like the Dreaming, like Hy Brasil, the Summer Country, Mythic Realms and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-22-2017, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T21:14:54-07:00","id":1106866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106788#post1106788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its all vague and contradictory. Appropriate for something related to dreams. The Maya are said to be pocket universes, ruled by powerful Umbrood called the Oneiroi. House Scathach had access to these worlds during the Interregnum.<br /> <br /> There is also other places mentioned that sound like the Dreaming, like Hy Brasil, the Summer Country, Mythic Realms and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Summer Country is from Werewolf, therefore Middle Umbral. There are paths between the Umbra and the Dreaming, but that tends to cement the two not being the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T02:50:56-07:00","id":1106931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106866#post1106866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Summer Country is from Werewolf, therefore Middle Umbral. There are paths between the Umbra and the Dreaming, but that tends to cement the two not being the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not necessarily, it seemed very much a unique place. Near Umbra could work, but it could actually be something else, and it does share some similarities with Arcadia or Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T03:31:36-07:00","id":1106941,"title":"","content":"Realms of all sorts connect via the Dreaming. You &quot;just&quot; need to find the path.<br /> <br /> So the Hsien can poke around the Dreaming without fear of Heavens wrath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-23-2017, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T03:44:37-07:00","id":1106944,"title":"","content":"Maybe. The \u201cno Spirit Worlds\u201d thing <i>might</i> conflate the Dreaming with the Umbra; it depends on whether allowing free access to the entire Dreaming would undermine the significance of the Jade Key. If it doesn't, then by all means let the Hsien have free run of the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T04:51:45-07:00","id":1106965,"title":"","content":"The intent is pretty clear, Hsien are banished from going beyond the Material. And the Umbra can be considered all non material portions of the Tellurian, hence why the Werewolves call the Underworld the Dark Umbra, even though it has nothing to do with the Penumbral Spirits. The Dreaming is only known as the Dreamzone, and due to Fae being really the only ones able to plunge deeply in it, Werewolves only know of the layer tapping into literal dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> But its pretty clear, if you want to leave the Material World you need the Jade Key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T07:09:42-07:00","id":1107000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106965#post1106965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But its pretty clear, if you want to leave the Material World you need the Jade Key.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true; intent matters. So perhaps the Hsien that C20 mentions in the Near Dreaming are simply the few enlightened ones with the Key-- At least the possibility of meeting an enlightened Hsien seems more common than running into a Siochain. It's &quot;simply&quot; a matter of mastering internal alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T08:11:14-07:00","id":1107017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106931#post1106931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well not necessarily, it seemed very much a unique place. Near Umbra could work, but it could actually be something else, and it does share some similarities with Arcadia or Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was listed as a Near Realm. It is in the Near Umbra, even if it is weird among the various places with similar distance from the Penumbra..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:33:56-07:00","id":1107036,"title":"","content":"Zones are described as being like a slice through a cake, touching all layers. This sounds about right for a description of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> But what of the Hsien and Horizen Realms or Shard Realms? They are material realms, with their own penumbra according to the Book of Worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-23-2017, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:29:07-07:00","id":1107103,"title":"","content":"Perhaps...<br /> Have you seen American Gods? On the very first chapter, Vikings had to engage into a mock war, sacrifice their right eyes and spill lots of blood to make Odin notice them since &quot;they were very far away&quot;. <br /> The Hsien mentioned were seen in San Francisco. <br /> Perhaps Heaven doesn't look that far away, either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:01:05-07:00","id":1107150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luisarmander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1107103#post1107103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps...<br /> Have you seen American Gods? On the very first chapter, Vikings had to engage into a mock war, sacrifice their right eyes and spill lots of blood to make Odin notice them since &amp;quot;they were very far away&amp;quot;. <br /> The Hsien mentioned were seen in San Francisco. <br /> Perhaps Heaven doesn't look that far away, either?</div> </div> </div> </div>American Gods has been an influence on my games. Especially regarding new dreams mixed with old. Lotto, sport mascots and old myths compete and meld. <br /> <br /> I reccommend Eight Days of Luke by Diana Wynne Jones. Norse legends and modern times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T23:59:35-07:00","id":1107235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1107000#post1107000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true; intent matters. So perhaps the Hsien that C20 mentions in the Near Dreaming are simply the few enlightened ones with the Key-- At least the possibility of meeting an enlightened Hsien seems more common than running into a Siochain. It's &quot;simply&quot; a matter of mastering internal alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is my take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:43:02-07:00","id":1114849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1102336-are-the-hsien-still-part-of-but-not-really-the-changeling-universe?p=1106167#post1106167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then let's go back to that. I think if the world of Changeling: the Dreaming has room for Inanimae, Dark-kin, &quot;tribal&quot; fae and Thallain, it surely has room for the Hsien.<br /> <br /> Now that I've had a few posts to think, I'm in favor of bringing the Hsien fundamentally in line with the other templates, while keeping their uniqueness as unchanged as possible. To me, this means the following additions to the Hsien template:<ul><li>A Permanent and Temporary Yugen track, which is the same as Glamour.</li> <li>A Permanent and Temporary Banality track (which, if we got to rename, I'd vote for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kegare\" target=\"_blank\">Kegare</a>).</li> <li>The ability to learn Arts and Realms, even if it isn't their default power set.</li> <li>The explicit ability to see and interact with chimerical reality.</li> </ul>The Hsien template's unique elements, lifted from the C20 text, would be:<ul><li>The kun shou, which requires that they incarnate in the bodies of the dying rather than in unborn children.</li> <li>The hotei and wani forms, which Hsien can apparently switch between at no cost, reflexively. The wani form triggers the Mists, and they get no chimerical seeming.</li> <li>Wu Tan, their default powers. Just as with Arts and Realms, any human-born fae (or Mannikin) should theoretically be able to learn Hsien alchemy, if they got the right teacher.</li> <li>Yin and Yang, which technically everyone has, but non-Hsien must be taught to awaken. A prerequisite for learning Wu Tan. (In systems terms, non-Hsien should only be able to buy chi values with freebies or experience.)</li> <li>The inability to go into any spirit world, unless the Hsien gets assistance or achieves enlightenment.</li> </ul>After all that's done, the only thing remaining on my wish list would be a &quot;How Do You DO That?&quot; style manual for alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like these suggestions! As a long-time Changeling Player/ST (since 1st edition) I've liked the idea of the Hsien but not the execution. They just seem too different from the kithain to work well in the same world. They don't even seem like &quot;fae&quot;, but more like minor godlings. I'll admit that my knowledge of such things is very Western, and I know little about Asian mythology, so they may fit well with that worldview. I've used them in my stories, but typically as single interactions because they don't mesh well with changelings. I know that from mindset and background they shouldn't mesh and mingle easily, but the game mechanics are so radically different that they don't mix any better than kithain do with mages or garou.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about doing a full rewrite on hsien to make them mechanically more similar to kithain, and I like Hsienfan's ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}